{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #879: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Call a set $S\\subseteq \\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$ admissible if $(a,b)=1$ for all $a\\neq b\\in S$. Let\\[G(n) = \\max_{S\\subseteq \\{1,\\ldots,n\\}} \\sum_{a\\in S}a\\]and\\[H(n)=\\sum_{p<n}p+ n\\pi(n^{1/2}).\\]Is it true that\\[G(n) >H(n)-n^{1+o(1)}?\\]Is it true that, for every $k\\geq 2$, if $n$ is sufficiently large then the admissible set which maximises $G(n)$ contains at least one integer with at least $k$ prime factors? Prize: no. OEIS: A186736. Tags: number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_4ad12f090608518b2b78ae0913b076d835f7194807d1b04929e8e62d5c58b56c","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:879","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_d942105535eb86bf","object_root":"sha256:7e8834b8b687c2bf54d8dd32c9e7bd79e035a06776592651db23e762a838d44c","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:879"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record